TridentBench — licence and attribution
======================================

This directory redistributes data derived from TridentBench.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Licence:                 MIT
Full licence text:       https://opensource.org/license/mit
Upstream dataset:        https://github.com/zackhuiiiii/TRIDENT

Citation
--------
Trident-Bench: Benchmarking LLM Safety in Law, Finance, and Medicine. COLM
(2026). https://github.com/zackhuiiiii/TRIDENT
[The upstream repository lists its arXiv identifier as TBD.]


Files in this directory
-----------------------
  tridentbench.json

Modifications
-------------
The data here is not the upstream distribution. It has been modified as follows,
and these changes are the responsibility of the Prj-BENCH authors, not the
upstream authors:

  - Converted to the common Prj-BENCH multiple-choice JSON schema
    (id / question / options / target / kind).
  - Medical subset. The nine AMA Principles of Medical Ethics used as a fixed option set; the harmful-prompt field used as the question stem with a fixed instruction appended.
  - Quality-control exclusions applied; see ../../_dropped_items.csv.

Licence basis
-------------
The upstream repository declares MIT via a "License: MIT" badge in its README,
but publishes no LICENSE file: both /blob/main/LICENSE and /blob/master/LICENSE
return HTTP 404 (verified 2026-08-20). No copyright year or holder is stated
anywhere upstream.

The standard MIT licence terms are therefore reproduced below for reference.
This text is NOT a verbatim copy of an upstream file, because no such file
exists, and the copyright line has deliberately been left unfilled — naming a
copyright holder is not ours to do. Anyone relying on this subset may wish to
ask the authors for an explicit LICENSE file.

